A||||7||DISenchanted||Well, one down...||||1||
Z||000000||DISenchanted||01-20-2000||02:55 AM||||First off, I'd like to thank everyone who replied about to the other post about the Salvaged title.  I've decided to look some more.<P>I was searching the internet today, and I ran across an ad.  87gt for sale.  That was all it said.  I gave it a call and it turns out that it was only 20 min away from here.  I drove out there after work and looked at it.<P>Wow.  I was actually impressed.  At first I thought that some one was trying to pull one over on me.  The paint needs work.  It is really oxidized.  If anyone can fix it I can.   I walked around tha car a few times.  It needs new dew wipes, that was it.<P>I got in the car and looked around for a while.  Almost perfect.<P>The lady came out and threw me the keys.  "TEST DRIVE!!!!!!"  I started her right up.  No problems what so ever.  Then I reached for the E-brake.  Something is not quite right there.  It was a pain to disenguage.  I reached for the gear shift.  Something is wrong there.  I've heard about some clip or something???  I got the hang of it, but it was not simple.  Down the road we went.<P>First off, there was a clicking coming from the dash.  I think it was the Trip Odometer.  I also noticed that it was out of alignment.  She said something about a bad bushing?  Not quite sure what she meant.<P>Ok, now here is where I need some help.  135,000 87 gt.  Needs the work mentioned above.  $2400???<P>Once again, thank you for your help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||JetroGT||01-20-2000||05:10 AM||||If you can paint the car your self, it's probably a dicient price. Every thing else sounds like minor problems. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||sdm1964||01-20-2000||06:33 AM||||It all sounds like all minor fixes, but maybe a little high on the price for the miles. I got my 85 GT with new paint, interior and needing nothing but a sunroof seal and wind deflector with 117,000 for $1500.00. But you also have to remember that prices vary in different places. If it is what you are wanting , talk them down and go for it.||||reg||14
Z||000003||AL||01-20-2000||09:22 PM||||i think it's t high for that car, try to bring her down i paid 900 for a red 86 gt look in the auto trader or keep lookin, good luck! AL. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||01-20-2000||09:33 PM||||I gave $2000 for my very used 88GT. I feel that is a little much, but it is what I wanted. If the car is what you want, then go for it. But, if it is not everything that you want in a Fiero, pass it by. I bought my 85 SE and it is a great car, but not exactly what I wanted. I added a fastback clip, poly suspension pieces, rear sway bar etc. . .but it still is not exactly what I wanted. So now I have 2 Fieros instead of 1. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||01-20-2000||11:12 PM||||My 2 cents;  I think that it is probably worth talking the seller down some.  My 86 gt came with recent clutch and 127k miles. It lasted 10k miles before I blew my engine. I paid $2500.  Personally I wouldn't really want to spend much less than that because of the hassles thatcome with; sagging door hinges, dessicated dew wipes, strange clicking in dash(? ruh roh!) If you have that kind of budget and want to get a car to drive, keep looking. If you want to have a hobby to work on, price her down and start buying parts. Again, just my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DISenchanted||01-21-2000||02:32 AM||||Ok, I tried to talk them down but they wouldn't budge.  I started looking through some classifieds, and I came across an 88gt.<P><BR>Automatic, no sun roof, no rear defoger, no performance sound, no rear wing.  Paint needs a little touch up.  Need the headlight motors rebuilt.  There was a small fire caused by the Egr.  Needs new egr, and various hoses and wires.  The engine was rebuilt 20,000 miles ago.  I can pick it up for $2200.  What about this one?||||reg||1
Z||000007||DISenchanted||01-21-2000||02:36 AM||||One more thing.  For anyone who has never driven an 88.  The ride is so much smoother, it's incredible.  I could not believe that this thing was a fiero.  I do believe that the greatly improved turning radius was a little exaggerated.  Either that or my litle 85gt was ahead of it's time.<P>The 88gt needs both quarter windows.||||reg||1
